    "short": "Dhanushkodi is the hauntingly beautiful ghost town at the southeastern tip of Pamban Island, Tamil Nadu, where the Bay of Bengal meets the Indian Ocean.",
    "description": "Dhanushkodi is a legendary abandoned coastal town situated on the narrow eastern tip of Pamban Island in Tamil Nadu. Flanked by the serene waters of the Bay of Bengal (Mahodadhi) on one side and the turbulent Indian Ocean (Ratnakara) on the other, Dhanushkodi is celebrated for Arichal Munai—the closest point to Sri Lanka—and the hauntingly picturesque ruins of its 1964 cyclone-destroyed church and railway terminus.",
